# Fledge GUI Project Architecture

## 🏗️ Project Overview
Fledge GUI is an Angular 16 application for IoT data management and monitoring with the following architecture:

- **Framework**: Angular 16 with TypeScript (strict mode enabled)
- **Build System**: Angular CLI with ngx-build-plus for module federation
- **Styling**: Bulma CSS framework with custom components
- **State Management**: RxJS BehaviorSubjects and services
- **Testing**: Jasmine/Karma for unit tests, Cypress for e2e testing

## 📁 Directory Structure

### Core Application Structure
```
src/app/
├── components/           # All UI components
│   ├── common/          # Reusable utility components
│   ├── core/            # Feature-specific components
│   └── layout/          # Layout and navigation components
├── services/            # Business logic and API services
├── guards/              # Route guards for access control
├── directives/          # Custom Angular directives
├── pipes/               # Custom transformation pipes
├── models/              # TypeScript interfaces and types
└── microfrontend/       # Module federation setup
```

### Component Organization Principles
- **common/**: Reusable UI components (alerts, modals, charts, pagination)
- **core/**: Feature modules (dashboard, configuration, logs, notifications)
- **layout/**: App shell components (navbar, sidebar, footer, login)

## 🔧 Key Technologies & Dependencies

### Core Dependencies
- **@angular/core**: ^16.2.12 (Angular framework)
- **rxjs**: ~6.6.6 (Reactive programming)
- **bulma**: ^0.9.4 (CSS framework)
- **chart.js**: ^4.3.0 (Data visualization)
- **moment**: ^2.29.3 (Date manipulation)

### Specialized Libraries
- **rete**: ^2.0.2 (Node-based visual editor)
- **@ali-hm/angular-tree-component**: Tree views
- **@ng-select/ng-select**: Enhanced select components
- **@ctrl/ngx-codemirror**: Code editor integration

## 🚀 Build & Development

### Scripts Reference
- `npm start`: Development server with git version preprocessing
- `npm run build`: Production build with optimization
- `npm run test`: Unit tests with Karma
- `npm run e2e`: Cypress end-to-end tests
- `npm run lint`: ESLint code analysis

### Module Federation
The application uses `@angular-architects/module-federation` for microfrontend architecture, enabling:
- Dynamic module loading
- Independent deployment of features
- Shared dependencies optimization

## 🔐 Authentication & Security
- Role-based access control (admin/data-view roles)
- Route guards for protected areas
- HTTP interceptors for request authentication

## 📊 Data Flow Patterns
- Services use BehaviorSubjects for reactive state management
- Components subscribe to service observables using async pipe
- Shared state via [SharedService](mdc:src/app/services/shared.service.ts)
- Ping service for connectivity monitoring and health checks